<ContentLayout title="About Aurora" description="About the Aurora computing ecosystem and its development." heading="About Aurora." lead="Aurora is an independent computing ecosystem centered on Aurora OS, with Lumen as its browser workstream.">
  <section class="section shell article-content">
    <h2>One ecosystem</h2>
    <p class="content-copy"><strong>Aurora OS</strong> is the foundation of the project: an operating system being built from scratch in Rust. <strong>Lumen</strong> is the browser workstream being developed alongside it. The aim is to build connected software with a coherent approach to security, privacy, reliability and user choice.</p>
    <h2>What matters to the project</h2>
    <div class="principle-grid">
      <article class="principle-card"><h3>Correctness</h3><p>Build behavior that can be specified, reviewed and tested.</p></article>
      <article class="principle-card"><h3>Security</h3><p>Make authority, privilege and trust boundaries explicit.</p></article>
      <article class="principle-card"><h3>Reliability</h3><p>Protect user data and communicate limitations clearly.</p></article>
      <article class="principle-card"><h3>Performance</h3><p>Measure resource use and latency rather than relying on assumptions.</p></article>
    </div>
    <h2>Current availability</h2>
    <p class="content-copy">Aurora is still in development. Neither Aurora OS nor Lumen has a public release. There are no public installers or user documentation yet.</p>
    <h2>Source code</h2>
    <p class="content-copy">The <a href="https://github.com/Pokejoueur/aurora-website" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Aurora Website repository</a> is public. The Aurora OS repository is private. The website will make product availability clear rather than suggesting that unreleased components are ready to use.</p>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>